## 🔄 BEFORE vs AFTER COMPARISON

### **BEFORE (Feature-Level Focus):**

```
Homepage Organization:
- Shows capabilities (VUS resolution, Guide design, etc.)
- Shows metrics (95.7% AUROC, etc.)
- Shows MOATs (S/P/E Framework, etc.)
- BUT: Doesn't show which products deliver these
- BUT: Doesn't organize by use case (Oncology, Drug Discovery)

Visitor Experience:
❌ Sees features but doesn't know which products provide them
❌ Doesn't understand: "I'm an oncologist, what do I use?"
❌ Can't connect capabilities to products
❌ Confused about product architecture
```

### **AFTER (Product-Level Focus):**

```
Homepage Organization:
- Shows products organized by use case ✅
  - Oncology Clinicians → Oracle + Command Center
  - Drug Discovery Researchers → Oracle + Forge + Boltz + Command Center
  - Research Scientists → Oracle + Command Center
- Shows capabilities with product attribution ✅
  - "S/P/E Framework powered by Oracle + Command Center"
  - "Target Validation powered by Oracle"
- Shows metrics with product attribution ✅
  - "Oracle: 95.7% AUROC"
  - "Forge: 70% Functional"

Visitor Experience:
✅ Sees products organized by use case
✅ Understands: "I'm an oncologist → Clinical Oncology tab → Oracle/Command Center"
✅ Can connect capabilities to products
✅ Clear product architecture understanding
✅ Can navigate to specific products for their use case
```

